  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-06-17T05:49:40.153Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I thought the Rift would be ideal for gestures triggering faces in VRChat, since that's something its controllers support more than the Vive (unless Knuckles get released).\n\nThe problem I'm running to, in addition to the gestures themselves being a little finicky, is that both hands are triggering them.  Which sounds nice in theory, but what it means in practice is that one hand must be kept in a neutral pose while the other gestures or the gestures will overlap.  I'm currently dealing with face animations, but I'm assuming this would affect other uses.\n\nCurrently, for HandOpen I have closed eyes and a wide open smile for when I wave, and for RockAndRoll I close my eyes a little bit and stick my tongue out.  If these trigger at the same time, my eyes close further than they should, and I have a solid wall of flesh where my eyes should be.  This problem would likely be worse if I installed more face animations.\n\nA good fix, which should be optional since some users might not want it, is to allow the left or right controller to be designated as the main-hand for gestures, while the off-hand won't trigger any (though ideally interacting with the world would still be possible).\n\nIt could be shown in options as a menu with 3 toggles: both, left, and right.  \"Both\" is for the current ambidextrous behavior, while \"left\" and \"right\" will toggle that respective controller as the main-hand for gestures.\n\nThis is a different, and kind of opposite, suggestion compared to what I've seen for having a separate gesture set for each hand.  To me, unless the Rift can offer more precise, easier to control gestures, having ANY gestures on my off-hand is a problem.   So if both suggestions were implemented, \"both\" would allow for both sets of gestures, but \"left\" or \"right\" would only allow for one set.",
